  <h1 class="page-title">Injury / Pain Log</h1>

  <div class="mb-5" id="view-explainer">
    <p class="text-[.95rem] text-foreground leading-[1.7]">A chronological log of climbs where you flagged pain or discomfort, plus any pattern in what's causing it.</p>
    <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted leading-[1.7] mt-2">Most recent first; each row shows the climb and the specific move(s) tagged. A ranked callout surfaces above the log once enough tags exist to spot a real pattern. Built from the <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">Pain/injury</strong> tags on each climb — a pattern-noticing tool, not medical advice.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="row-card text-center max-w-[420px] mx-auto" id="performance-offline" hidden>
    <p class="text-[.9rem] text-foreground">Performance insights need a connection.</p>
    <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted mt-2">Reconnect and reload this page to see your injury/pain log.</p>
  </div>

  <div id="injury-log-root"></div>

  <h2 class="sources-heading">Sources</h2>
  <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted leading-[1.7] mb-3">Finger flexor pulley injuries are the most common overuse injury in climbers, which is why this view exists as a pattern-spotting tool rather than a diagnostic one:</p>
  <ol class="m-0 pl-[1.2rem] text-[.84rem] leading-[1.6] text-foreground [&>li+li]:mt-[10px]">
